%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
%   PUBLICATIONS — Benedikt Brückner
%   Single source of truth. build.py generates the website's publication list
%   and every BibTeX button from this file.
%
%   THIS FILE IS PUBLIC. It is committed to a public GitHub repository, so it
%   is readable by anyone, indexed by GitHub search, and mirrored by
%   code-search sites — independently of what the deployed page shows.
%   Therefore: never add work that is under review. Some venues object to
%   authors stating publicly that a paper is under submission with them, and
%   omitting it from the rendered page is not enough when the source is
%   public. Under-review work belongs in the CV, which is not published.
%   build.py refuses to build if it finds such an entry.
%
%   FORMAT POLICY — deliberately the opposite of the papers-repo bib.bib.
%   That file serves Benedikt's own bibliographies, where a house style
%   applies. This one serves OTHER PEOPLE's, so it is maximally complete:
%
%     - Full given names, never initials. A style can abbreviate "Benedikt
%       Brückner" to "B. Brückner" automatically; nothing can expand "B."
%       back, so abbreviating destroys information.
%     - Canonical DBLP booktitles, including location and dates. Verbose, but
%       it is the authoritative record and downstream can always trim.
%     - DOI, pages, series, volume, publisher and editors where known.
%       Unused fields are silently dropped by styles that don't want them.
%     - arXiv eprints alongside published DOIs, so readers can reach a free
%       copy even when the DOI sits behind a publisher.
%     - Umlauts as {\"u}: works under pdfLaTeX, XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX alike.
%     - Acronyms braced ({IoUCert}, {AAAI}, {YOLO}) so styles that lowercase
%       titles cannot mangle them.
%     - Conventional lowercase surname+year+keyword keys, since they end up
%       pasted into strangers' .tex files.
%     - No bibsource/biburl/timestamp: DBLP bookkeeping, not bibliography.
%
%   NON-STANDARD DISPLAY FIELDS — used by build.py for the web page and
%   STRIPPED from the BibTeX shown by the copy buttons, so nobody pastes them:
%     shortvenue  human-readable venue label for the page ("AAAI 2025")
%     status      badge: preprint | workshop. There is no under-review value:
%                 build.py rejects it outright, per the warning above.
%     equal       1-indexed authors sharing an equal-contribution asterisk
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

